    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i have a 2018 honda civic and every time i hit the gas there is this really loud squealing noise coming from under the hood. can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt, or drive belt, is a crucial component in your 2018 Civic, as it transfers power from the engine's crankshaft to various accessories. It's responsible for spinning things like the alternator (which charges the battery), the power steering pump, and the air conditioning compressor. If this belt is worn out or slipping, it can create a loud squealing noise, which is a sign that the belt is struggling to grip the pulleys. It's a common issue, and replacing the belt or checking the tensioners is usually the fix.",
      "source": "target",
