    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for explaining that. so if the belt is just slipping it makes that sound, but do you think it could be something else like a pulley or the tensioner itself? i'm trying to figure out if i can just swap the belt or if i'm looking at a bigger repair.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Squealing can certainly be a sign of a slipping belt, but you are right to consider other culprits; a bad pulley or a failing tensioner can produce a similar, high-pitched whine, sometimes even louder than a simple belt slip. If the belt itself looks glazed, cracked, or frayed, replacing just the belt is likely the cheapest fix. However, if the noise persists after a new belt goes on, the tensioner bearing might be seizing up, which would require replacing the tensioner assembly. It's a good idea to have a mechanic take a look to pinpoint the exact source of the noise.",
      "source": "target",
