      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Inconsistent noise is often a telltale sign of a system that is under stress, like a belt system that is starting to fail. When the belt is slightly loose or the tensioner is just starting to fail, the slippage might only happen under specific load—like when you aggressively step on the gas, which forces the accessories to work harder. It's not entirely normal, but it does happen as components wear down, which is why it's wise to get it looked at before it becomes a full-blown, catastrophic failure. A failing pulley bearing, for instance, might only squeal when it spins at a certain speed.",
